1
00:00:01,220 --> 00:00:03,660
Imagine that a year from now,

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:06,060
your life could be completely different.

3
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,820
You could become smarter,

4
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:10,460
learn new things, build useful habits,

5
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:12,920
and move closer to your dream.

6
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:15,760
But there is one problem.

7
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:18,900
You think that to do this,

8
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:20,860
you need something huge:

9
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:22,680
to completely change your daily

10
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:24,800
routine, find motivation,

11
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:27,340
and start a new life on Monday.

12
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:29,300
And that is exactly why

13
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:31,280
most people never start.

14
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:32,780
They wait for big changes,

15
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,140
and miss the power of small actions.

16
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:40,040
In the book Atomic Habits, James Clear

17
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:42,840
explains that big changes often begin

18
00:00:42,860 --> 00:00:46,440
with small actions you repeat every day.

19
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Think about it. You don't have to read

20
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:52,620
an entire book in one evening.

21
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:54,680
Start with a few pages.

22
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:57,680
You don't have to train for two hours.

23
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:00,140
Start with a few minutes of movement.

24
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:01,140
You don't need to change

25
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:03,300
your whole life at once.

26
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:05,400
Choose one habit, and gradually

27
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:07,440
make it part of your day.

28
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:10,620
At first, the results

29
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:12,640
will be almost invisible.

30
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:13,680
You might even feel

31
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:15,740
that nothing is changing.

32
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:18,140
But it is repetition that builds

33
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:20,710
the foundation for progress.

34
00:01:20,730 --> 00:01:23,100
And remember: you don't have to become

35
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:25,440
a different person in one day.

36
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,620
What matters is taking at least one

37
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:30,240
step in the right direction, every day.

38
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:31,940
Because your future life

39
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:34,800
is built from what you do today.

40
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:39,440
So here is the question.

41
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:43,780
What one small habit are you ready to start today?

